      "level": 1,
      "content": "Nested Loops"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It's possible to put a loop inside another loop. This is known as a nested loop."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In a nested loop, the inner loop is executed for each iteration of the outer loop. Let's try to understand it with the help of an example."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1attributes = ['Electric', 'Fast']\n2cars = ['Tesla', 'Porsche', 'Mercedes']\n3\n4for attribute in attributes:\n5    for car in cars:\n6        print(attribute, car)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Electric Tesla\nElectric Porsche\nElectric Mercedes\nFast Tesla\nFast Porsche\nFast Mercedes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, the inner loop is iterated once for each item of the attributes list. Here's how this code works:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "First iteration of the outer loop"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        [
